id: hac-8h2c
title: Non-interactive setup wizard corrupts structured stdout
description: "The settings wizard writes human banners, progress lines, and prose around formatter-selected output, so --format json or json-compact cannot be parsed and other advertised formats are not honored as single programmatic receipts."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags[6]: agents,cli,formatters,regression,setup-wizard,stdout
created_at: "2026-08-07T19:37:57.246Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T19:37:57.246Z"
deadline: "2026-08-09T19:37:57.246Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Every non-interactive formatter emits one valid parseable receipt without human prefix/suffix lines; Connection success and failure are represented in the receipt without token, raw URL, location name, or other private values; Interactive wizard guidance remains intuitive and isolated config/auth/data files retain secure permissions"
definition_of_ready: Isolated reproduction completed against live Core 2026.7.4; current wizard implementation and tests inspected; formatter utilities available
goal: machine-safe-cli-bootstrap
objective: strict-noninteractive-wizard-output
value: CI and agents can configure hassio without brittle stdout scraping.
impact: Removes a hard parser failure from the mandatory setup path and prevents accidental private-value logging.
outcome: One deterministic setup receipt across all six supported formats with regression tests and live isolated acceptance.
why_now: The user explicitly requires a fully working setup wizard and valid programmatic output; current behavior fails strict JSON parsing.
parent: hac-zdp4
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 100
sprint: api-parity-2026-08
release: unreleased
severity: high
environment: "homeassistant-cli 2026.8.6, Bun, non-interactive wizard, isolated HASSIO_CONFIG, live Home Assistant Core 2026.7.4"
repro_steps: "Run hassio settings wizard --non-interactive with isolated HASSIO_CONFIG, environment token, valid URL, --config-read-only true, and --format json-compact; parse stdout with JSON.parse."
expected_result: "stdout is exactly one valid JSON object describing saved paths, read-only mode, and connection outcome without secrets."
actual_result: "stdout begins with a SETUP WIZARD banner and multiple human lines, causing JSON.parse to throw before any receipt can be consumed."
affected_version: 2026.8.6
component: settings-wizard
regression: true
customer_impact: Automated bootstrap and agent workflows cannot safely consume the advertised structured format.
